WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.467
Today is the middle sound. It is the hardest one to hear, so go slowly.

2
00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:11.729
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:12.229 --> 00:00:14.808
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:17.388
Say the name of every picture first.

5
00:00:17.838 --> 00:00:22.518
The middle sound is the one you can sing. Say the word slowly, and hold the middle.

6
00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.003
The word is cat.

7
00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:26.625
The word is sun.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.224
The word is pig.

9
00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:37.310
If your child cannot find it, pull the whole word apart with the counters. The middle counter is the middle sound.

10
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.815
The word is dog.

11
00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:48.064
Your child says the middle sound of the six pictures in job one, and marks each box.

12
00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:56.305
In job two, your child circles the picture with the same middle sound as the first one. Then checks the answers upside down.

13
00:00:56.755 --> 00:01:01.724
Then turn to the rhyme story. Read each line out loud, and stop before the picture.

14
00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:05.808
Your child says the last word. Then ask which two words rhyme.
